If your measurements are accurate, the result means the 5 kg was not all inside you at the second weighing. The likely explanations are:

- you didn’t actually ingest 5 kg (spilled, vomited, or “5 kg” was an estimate);
- mass left before you weighed: urine, sweat, breath, feces, or bleeding;
- scale/timing error: not zeroed, different scale, floor, resolution, or you moved;
- “instantly” meant minutes, during which some water/CO₂ can be lost.

Normal breathing/sweating over a few minutes can remove maybe 0.1–0.5 kg, not 5 kg. So if the gap is large, the most probable cause is measurement or ingestion error.

